8
00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:32.000
Equivalence is closely
related to implication.

9
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.900
Two statements are said to be equivalent,
or

10
00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:39.360
more fully, logically equivalent,
if each implies the other.

11
00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:41.580
Equivalence is a central
notion in mathematics.

12
00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:46.550
Many mathematical results are proofs
that two statements are equivalent.

13
00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:53.040
In fact, equivalence is to logic as
equations are to arithmetic and algebra.

14
00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:57.470
And you already know that equations
play a central role in mathematics.

15
00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:04.160
Just as we had to introduce
a formal version of implication

16
00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:08.660
that avoids the complex issue of
causation, namely the conditional,

17
00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:12.960
we have to introduce an analogous
version of equivalence.

18
00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:15.230
It's called the biconditional.

19
00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:20.070
Fortunately, we did all
the difficult work with implication.

20
00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:23.430
Now we can reap the benefits
of those efforts.

21
00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:29.120
Two statements phi and psi are said
to be logically equivalent, or

22
00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:31.580
just equivalent,
if each implies the other.

23
00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:36.360
Since we have a formal
version of implication,

24
00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:40.830
named the conditional, it follows that
there's a formal version of equivalence.

25
00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:42.671
We call it the biconditional.

26
00:01:45.968 --> 00:01:48.050
The biconditional of phi and

27
00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:52.660
psi is denoted by means of
a double-headed arrow, like this.

28
00:01:55.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Formally, the biconditional is
an abbreviation of phi conditional psi and

29
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.190
psi conditional phi.

30
00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:09.960
Since the conditional is defined
in terms of truth values,

31
00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:13.380
it follows that the biconditional is
defined in terms of truth values.

32
00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:19.900
If you work out the truth table for
phi conditional psi and for

33
00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:23.430
psi conditional phi and
then you work out the conjunction,

34
00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:26.840
you'll get the truth table for
phi biconditional psi.

35
00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:34.930
And if you do that, what you will find
is that phi biconditional psi is true,

36
00:02:34.930 --> 00:02:38.050
if phi and psi are both true or
if they're both false.

37
00:02:40.130 --> 00:02:42.000
One way to show that two statement phi and

38
00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:45.360
psi are equivalent is to show
