00:17:15.903 --> 00:17:20.600
To be necessary, n being a multiple
of 10 has to imply the statement.

240
00:17:22.160 --> 00:17:22.981
Well let's see.

241
00:17:26.191 --> 00:17:31.400
Does n being a multiple of 10
imply that it's a multiple of 5?

242
00:17:31.400 --> 00:17:33.510
Yes it does, so that one's necessary.

243
00:17:37.290 --> 00:17:42.790
Does n being a multiple of 10
imply this is a multiple of 20?

244
00:17:43.830 --> 00:17:45.270
10 is itself a multiple of 10.

245
00:17:46.696 --> 00:17:48.603
But 10 is certainly not a multiple of 20.

246
00:17:53.475 --> 00:17:59.282
Does n being multiple of 10 imply that n
is even and that it's a multiple of 5?

247
00:17:59.282 --> 00:18:05.511
Yes, does n being a multiple of 10
imply that it's a multiple of 100?

248
00:18:05.511 --> 00:18:11.770
No, does n being a multiple of 10 imply
that n squared is a multiple of 100?

249
00:18:11.770 --> 00:18:16.566
Yes, so the three conditions
that are necessary for

250
00:18:16.566 --> 00:18:19.947
the number n to be a multiple of 10.

251
00:18:19.947 --> 00:18:26.070
Condition one, condition three,
condition five.

252
00:18:26.070 --> 00:18:27.355
Okay, let's move on to Part 2.

